{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/230715-the-merit-clear-sighted","id":230715,"title":"The Merit Clear Sighted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-16T17:26:59-07:00","id":230715,"title":"The Merit Clear Sighted","content":"The merit clear sighted in the book Hunter Hunted allow a character to see through a vampires obfuscate with a Per + Alert roll vs Obfuscate level +3. What I need to know is how does this merit work verses other supernaturals? Is it the same roll only change obfuscate for the power used? Any help or ideas would be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T18:51:49-07:00","id":230808,"title":"","content":"Well, it says, &quot;When faced with a supernatural illusion, such as those created by Obfuscate, Chimerstry, and the like...&quot; which means that this works with anything that qualifies as a &quot;supernatural illusion&quot;. So, most Sphere magick effects using Forces or Mind to create illusions, or Fera Gifts that create illusions... These would all allow a roll to see through them. And yes, the roll is the same, as described in the merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T18:52:59-07:00","id":230810,"title":"","content":"&quot;As described in the merit&quot; meaning a difficulty of the power's level + 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T19:02:22-07:00","id":230817,"title":"","content":"Would it allow the character to perceive a Changelings Fae Mein? What would be the roll, since it isn't a power with a level. Would it be the changelings willpower? Thanks for the input so far, it helps a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T19:42:19-07:00","id":230879,"title":"","content":"Hm... I have no idea. I'm not well-versed in Changeling. My initial reaction would be &quot;no&quot;, because the &quot;real world&quot; appearance of the Changeling doesn't seem like an illusion to be pierced. We might need someone else's input on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/av